 National Park"," ","is known for extremes: It is North America’s driest and hottest spot (with fewer than two inches/five centimeters of rainfall annually and a record high of 134°F), and has the lowest elevation on the continent—282 feet below sea level."]},{"type":"h2","content":["10."," ",{"type":"a","content":["Redwood National Park"],"attrs":{"href":"https://www.nationalgeographic.com/travel/national-parks/article/redwood-national-park","target":"_blank","dir":"ltr"}},", California"]}],{"type":"inline","content":{"name":"Image","props":{"link":{},"caption":{"title":"","credit":"Photograph by Jonathan Irish","source":"","text":"Sunrise in the middle of the Redwood Forest in Redwood National Park, California","lines":3,"showMoreText":"Read More","showLess":false},"image":{"id":"Redwood National Park, California","showCopyright":"Please be respectful of copyright. Unauthorized use is prohibited.","alt":"sunrise in the middle of the redwood forest in Redwood National Park, California","src":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg","sources":[{"src":{"x1":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=374&h=249","x2":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=748&h=498"},"max":374,"nativeWidth":374},{"src":{"x1":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=413&h=275","x2":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=826&h=550"},"max":413,"min":375,"nativeWidth":413},{"src":{"x1":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=767&h=511","x2":"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/5b1a4b25-48a9-4dbd-bdd3-3d4240871d8e/redwood-national-park-sunrise-forest.jpg?w=1534&h=1022"},"max":767,"min":414,"nativeWidth":767},{"src":{